+# Matching verifier rollout â€” 2026-10-12
+
+Owner reports that the app still says it does not match the backend after deployment. Requirement IDs B01/B05/B07, R01, SB01â€“SB05, Q01. The preceding Studio rollout incorrectly left the racing mismatch unresolved: public `/v1/manifest` returned compiler22/physics53 while the current client uses compiler25/physics54. Engine, five-lap rules and track schema already matched.
+
+Deploy a frozen canonical verifier overlay over the exact Studio release parent. Preserve its backend source, schema30, API settings, secrets, resources and single worker. Add `speed_bumps` to `backend/deploy/stage_verifier.py` so the stripped verifier includes the current simulation dependency. Immutable official-track revisions acquire the current validated manifests; do not rewrite historical track manifests, boards, scores or rivalry contracts. Current-week membership keys already include the full build contract, so newly entered competitions use the matching cohort.
+
+Changed source files: `backend/deploy/stage_verifier.py`, `backend/tests/test_verifier.py`, `backend/tests/fixtures/verified_oval.json`; deployment helper `.tools/matching_verifier_rollout_20261012.py`; this report and status/phase entries. The previous oval fixture is preserved in `docs/evidence/matching-verifier-deploy-2026-10-12/verified-oval-before.json`. Current manifest/hash fixture updates follow actual Windows and Linux execution; all lap/timing/rejection assertions remain. Historical handbrake migration still targets physics53 and is not relabelled to54.
